              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to cave in, then the Marathi for a landslide."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पूर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पूर — pūr — \"a flood\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नदीला पूर आल्यास हा पूल बंद होईल. nadīlā pūr ālyās hā pūl band hoīl. Should the river flood, this bridge will be closed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नदीला पूर (pūr) येणे, the river floods; आल्यास, should it come."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पूर (pūr) goes back to Sanskrit pūra, 'filling; a flood': CDIAL lists the Marathi word, as purā, 'filling; flood', under it (CDIAL 8330)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
